  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Photo Release Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a photo release form?\", \"a\": \"A photo release form gives an organization signed permission to publish pictures of a person in the places the form names. Good ones list each use and say how long the permission runs. When the subject is a child, a parent or guardian signs.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a photo release form?\", \"a\": \"Settle the wording first: the uses you need and how someone withdraws. Then describe the release to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>. It builds a form with a checkbox per use and a separate page for parents, and keeps each signed release in your database.\"}, {\"q\": \"Do I need a photo release form?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if you plan to use someone's picture to advertise or sell something. New York law requires written consent for advertising or trade use, given by a parent or guardian for a minor. California requires prior consent for advertising use and exempts news, public affairs and sports coverage.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a picture release form include?\", \"a\": \"A picture release form should name the person and the organization and list each permitted use. Add the term and any payment, then explain how to withdraw. It closes with a signature and a date, plus a parent's name and relationship when the subject is a minor.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can you provide an example of a photo release form?\", \"a\": \"Here is a sample photo release form for a school: \\\"I give Ambleside Elementary permission to photograph my child, Leo Arkin. The school may use the photos in the yearbook and on its website until I withdraw this permission in writing.\\\" The parent signs and dates it below.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a media release form and a photo release form?\", \"a\": \"Scope. A media release form covers video and voice recordings as well as still pictures, which suits press interviews and testimonials. A photo release covers pictures alone. Neither replaces a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/liability-waiver-form'>liability waiver form</a>, which releases an organizer from certain claims over injuries at an activity.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the time limit on a photo release consent form?\", \"a\": \"No single limit applies. It runs for the term written into it. Schools often collect a new photo release consent form each year at enrollment, while a release for one event can run until the signer withdraws. Keep the signed record for as long as the photos stay in use. An Emergent form files each release in a database you own, next to the date it was signed.\"}, {\"q\": \"Is a sample photo release form enough on its own?\", \"a\": \"Rarely. A sample photo release form gives you wording to adapt. Swap its uses for the places your pictures will run, set the age below which a parent signs, and add how someone withdraws. Because state laws differ, have a lawyer read the final version.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the rule for signing a photo consent form for a minor?\", \"a\": \"A parent or legal guardian signs, and the form records the child's name beside theirs. Many schools collect a photo consent form at enrollment for the whole year, and others fold the question into a broader consent form. With no response cap, an Emergent form can take a release for every child in a district.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one form include video, or do you need a video release form?\", \"a\": \"One form can cover both when it names video and sound recordings alongside still pictures and gives each use its own checkbox. A standalone video release form fits interviews and testimonials, where a person's voice and words are used as well as their face.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
}